# Byte-exactness guarantee for replication.
# Every committed artifact (JSON outputs, CSV fixtures, lock files, markdown)
# participates in md5/byte-identity checks: verify.py's embedded-input hashes,
# the rerun gate's regenerated-vs-committed byte comparison, and e12's runtime
# LEG-A artifact guard. Git line-ending translation (core.autocrlf) rewrites
# LF to CRLF at checkout on default Windows git, silently changing on-disk
# bytes and turning all of those checks RED on a fresh clone (found by the
# Phase 5b clean-room reproduction, 2026-07-28). Declaring every path -text
# disables translation entirely: what is committed is what checks out.
* -text
